/*
:name: clock_or_data
:type: error
:tolg: 1
:error: `clk` is a `Clock`, and a Clock is not data \(operator `or`\)
*/
// todo/livehd/2f-latch M9 — NOTHING MAY BE DONE TO A CLOCK except a recognized
// clock operation, and the only one is the gate `Clock(clock_pin=clk,
// enable=en)` (a Clock_cell, ruling 56); there are no derived clocks (qa.md
// Appendix 6).
//
// `clk or sel` has no meaning as a clock, and getting it wrong is SILENT rather
// than loud: a step-granular formal encoder has no clock-identity model, so an
// OR of a clock with data looks exactly like the bare clock and the design came
// back PROVEN equal to an ungated one. With `clk` typed `Clock` it is caught at
// the operator, where the source span still exists to point at.
pub mod bad_clock(clk:Clock, sel:Bool, d:U8) -> (q:U8@[1]) {
  const gclk = clk or sel   // locate_error_here
  reg f:U8:[clock_pin=gclk] = 0
  q = f
  f = d
}
